{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "62386c9c-a54c-8249-a84d-c4e64700bcc1",
  "created_at": "2025-12-09T13:28:27-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Edson Gomes",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Priya Raman",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:25:50-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Water and sewer billing, this is Priya. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:25:55-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah, good afternoon. I'm calling about my water bill, I think it's the water bill. It says it's for, um, a whole quarter? Like three months? I don't get why it's not monthly."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:26:07-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. Water and sewer are billed quarterly, so each bill covers about three months of usage. Do you have the bill in front of you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:26:16-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I do, I do. [pause] Okay, it says service from September something to, uh, December something. How do they count the dates? Is that when I used it, or when they read it? Sorry, I'm on speakerphone, can you hear me okay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:26:31-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you fine. The dates on the bill are the meter reading dates. The period runs from the previous reading to the most recent reading, so it's the usage between those two reads, not the date it was mailed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:26:45-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ohh, so the mail date is a different thing. Okay. So the, the reading date is the end of the period, and the due date is after that. Wait, no, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:26:57-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right. Reading date closes the period, the bill is generated afterward, and the due date is printed separately near the top."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:27:05-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. Okay. And the name on it is my wife's name, she passed, and I never changed it. Is that a problem? I'm at 218 Kay Street, by the way, I should've said that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:27:17-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. It's not a problem for paying. If you'd like the account put in your name, we can send you the form for that. I can note that on the account today."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:27:29-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, please, do that. Um, and can I ask, if I can't get down there during the day, is there a drop box? Like for after the office closes? I'm trying to remember, I had another question, hang on. [laughs] Lost it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:27:43-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No rush. Yes, there's a payment drop box at City Hall that you can use outside office hours. Put a check or money order in with the payment stub from your bill, and write your account number on the check."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:27:57-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, check, stub, account number. Sorry, one sec. [pause] My buddy just showed up, didn't even text me, he's sitting in the next room waiting. I should wrap this up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:28:08-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Of course. I'll note the name change request and mail the form to the Kay Street address. Anything else on the bill?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:28:16-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, I think that's it. The quarter thing, the reading dates, the box. I think I got it. Mostly. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-09T13:28:24-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. Have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
